# results/, which is already ignored, but a stray run can drop one here.
results.html

# --- Local scratch notes, not part of the repo ---
REMOTE.md

# --- Benchmark output ---
#
# Ignored by default: a results/ directory is per-machine, and a laptop run and
# a rented-box run must not overwrite each other. What earns a commit is a
# measurement a document cites; the 350 KB compiler transcripts from building
# flash-attn and bootstrapping the box do not. Those prove a build happened,
# which no document claims.
#
# LAYOUT. `results/<card>/{data,figures,logs}/`, card first, because the card
# is the axis a measurement cannot be read without. A path names its own
# provenance, and two cards can hold files of the same name without colliding
# -- which matters because `triton.testing` writes a fixed set of names.
#
# Three ordering rules make this work, and each one silently broke it once:
#
# 1. Exclude the *contents*, never the directory. Git does not descend into an
#    excluded directory, so a negation under one is dead text. `!results/**/`
#    re-includes every directory so the file negations below are reachable at
#    all. Dropping that one line un-tracks the entire tree.
# 2. `**` rather than `*`, because the files now sit three levels down. The
#    previous block matched one level and would miss every one of them.
# 3. This block sits at the end of the file. The last matching pattern wins,
#    and `*.csv` / `*.png` under "Benchmark scratch" above would otherwise
#    re-ignore every figure and measurement un-ignored here.
results/**
!results/**/
!results/**/*.csv
!results/**/*.json
!results/**/*.png
!results/**/*.md
!results/*/logs/*.log
!results/*/logs/*.txt

# Re-excluded after the negations above, deliberately: build transcripts, not
# measurements. 692 KB between them and nothing cites either.
results/*/logs/bootstrap.log
results/*/logs/fa283-build.log
